## Task contract

Create `{{ variants_dir }}/<variant_id>/reader.json` using
`{{ task_dir }}/assets/harness/reader.schema.json`. The directory may contain
only that JSON file. Do not add code, prompt text, paths, model material, labels,
or undeclared fields.

Run preliminary synchronously:

```bash
"$PRAXIST_TASK_PYTHON" {{ task_dir }}/evaluations/cross_view/run.py \
  --variant-dir {{ variants_dir }}/<variant_id> \
  --output-dir {{ results_dir }}/<variant_id>/preliminary \
  --mode preliminary
```

Submit complete evaluation through the scheduler with a stable semantic tag:

```bash
PYTHONPATH="$PRAXIST_WORKSPACE_ROOT${PYTHONPATH:+:$PYTHONPATH}" \
  "$PRAXIST_RUNNER_PYTHON" -m praxist.plugins.workflow_stages.research_loop.backend.protected_pids launch \
  --run-dir={{ run_dir }} --peer={{ peer_id }} \
  --tag=<variant_identity> --profile=mps_readout --work-class=mature --eta=60 -- \
  "$PRAXIST_TASK_PYTHON" {{ task_dir }}/evaluations/cross_view/run.py \
  --variant-dir {{ variants_dir }}/<variant_id> \
  --output-dir {{ results_dir }}/<variant_id>/complete \
  --mode complete
```

Repeated ordinary submissions are idempotent. After repairing a terminal
failed or rejected request, keep the tag and add `--retry-terminal`; never use
that flag for active or completed work. Do not use raw background processes,
`nohup`, arbitrary polling, or private transcript size as completion evidence.

Publish summary path, actual metrics, exit classification, effort/coverage,
failure mode, evidence valence, and actual design dimensions. A development
PASS only nominates a loop-external formal validation; it never authorizes
candidate import, owner publication, PE/credit, ModificationGate, SHADOW, or
ACTIVE.
